---
// src/components/HowItWorks.astro
---

<section class="how-section" id="how-it-works">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-header">
      <span class="badge badge-brand">Architecture Pipeline</span>
      <h2 class="section-title">How SpeedFlow Accelerates Downloads</h2>
      <p class="section-subtitle">
        Understanding the multi-threaded range pipeline from remote URL ingestion to on-disk chunk assembly.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- 4-Stage Flat Pipeline -->
    <div class="pipeline-container grid-hairline">
      <!-- Step 1 -->
      <div class="step-card">
        <div class="step-top">
          <span class="step-num font-mono">01</span>
          <span class="badge">Handshake</span>
        </div>
        <h3 class="step-title">Server Capability Discovery</h3>
        <p class="step-desc">
          SpeedFlow sends a non-destructive HEAD request to examine HTTP response headers. It checks for <code>Accept-Ranges: bytes</code>, confirms total byte length, and records the server's <code>ETag</code> for safe resumption.
        </p>
        <div class="code-snippet font-mono">
          <span class="code-comment">// Remote Server Response</span>
          <span>HTTP/2 206 Partial Content</span>
          <span>Accept-Ranges: bytes</span>
          <span>Content-Length: 4294967296</span>
          <span>ETag: "63e18a-100000000"</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Step 2 -->
      <div class="step-card">
        <div class="step-top">
          <span class="step-num font-mono">02</span>
          <span class="step-badge badge">Segmentation</span>
        </div>
        <h3 class="step-title">Range Partitioning & Pre-allocation</h3>
        <p class="step-desc">
          The file is mathematically partitioned into equal, non-overlapping byte ranges. A sparse file container is allocated on disk so each async worker writes directly to its designated position without intermediate copies.
        </p>
        <div class="code-snippet font-mono">
          <span class="code-comment">// Tokio Segment Allocation</span>
          <span>Seg #0: [000000000 - 0268435455]</span>
          <span>Seg #1: [0268435456 - 0536870911]</span>
          <span>...</span>
          <span>Seg #15: [4026531840 - 4294967295]</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Step 3 -->
      <div class="step-card">
        <div class="step-top">
          <span class="step-num font-mono">03</span>
          <span class="step-badge badge">Concurrency</span>
        </div>
        <h3 class="step-title">Parallel Async Worker Execution</h3>
        <p class="step-desc">
          Tokio spawns independent worker tasks. Each worker requests its assigned range through an isolated HTTP connection, bypassing single-thread network throttles applied by CDNs and edge servers.
        </p>
        <div class="code-snippet font-mono">
          <span class="code-comment">// Async Range Streams</span>
          <span>Worker-01 &lt;-- HTTP Stream 1 [ACTIVE]</span>
          <span>Worker-02 &lt;-- HTTP Stream 2 [ACTIVE]</span>
          <span>Worker-16 &lt;-- HTTP Stream 16 [ACTIVE]</span>
          <span class="text-brand">Throughput Aggregated: 48.2 MB/s</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Step 4 -->
      <div class="step-card">
        <div class="step-top">
          <span class="step-num font-mono">04</span>
          <span class="step-badge badge">Verification</span>
        </div>
        <h3 class="step-title">Atomic Finalization & SHA-256</h3>
        <p class="step-desc">
          When the final segment finishes, temporary handles are flushed and closed. SpeedFlow performs an atomic file rename, computes a streaming SHA-256 digest, and notifies the desktop UI and OS shell.
        </p>
        <div class="code-snippet font-mono">
          <span class="code-comment">// Integrity & Local State</span>
          <span>Integrity: SHA-256 Validated</span>
          <span>Target: C:\Downloads\archive.iso</span>
          <span class="text-brand">SQLite Task Status: COMPLETED (0ms)</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .how-section {
    padding: 64px 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    background-color: var(--surface-secondary);
  }

  .section-header {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    text-align: center;
    gap: 12px;
    max-width: 680px;
    margin: 0 auto 40px auto;
  }

  .section-title {
    font-size: clamp(22px, 3.2vw, 32px);
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    color: var(--text-primary);
  }

  .section-subtitle {
    font-size: 14px;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.5;
  }

  .pipeline-container {
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
  }

  .step-card {
    padding: 24px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 12px;
    background-color: var(--surface);
  }

  .step-top {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
  }

  .step-num {
    font-size: 20px;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--brand-primary);
  }

  .step-title {
    font-size: 15px;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--text-primary);
  }

  .step-desc {
    font-size: 12px;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .step-desc code {
    background-color: var(--surface-secondary);
    padding: 2px 4px;
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    font-size: 11px;
    color: var(--brand-primary);
  }

  .code-snippet {
    background-color: var(--surface-secondary);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    padding: 10px 12px;
    font-size: 11px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 3px;
    color: var(--text-primary);
    overflow-x: auto;
  }

  .code-comment {
    color: var(--text-tertiary);
  }

  .text-brand {
    color: var(--brand-primary);
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .pipeline-container {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
